Original commit body from b9e6c34:

Go web frameworks (Gin, Echo, Fiber) use method calls (r.GET, e.POST)
for route registration, not decorators. This is the same pattern as
Django and Express - function/method calls rather than decorators.

These cannot be migrated to the current YAML pattern system which only
matches decorator/base_class metadata on symbols. The UsageContext model
in ADR-0003 proposes a future solution for call-based patterns.

Changes:
- Added clarifying comments to Go analyzer
- Updated go-web.yaml to note decorator patterns are placeholders
- Updated spec v1.0.x status
